object:
  title: Southern Digital Justice Comparison Lens
  type: option-entry
  category: knowledge-documentation
  what_it_is: Compare digital systems using regional political economy, colonial history, gender, labor, publicness, rights, infrastructure and community power rather than importing one universal responsible-tech frame.
  potential_uses: AI governance, data policy, DPI, platform regulation, public-interest technology and source-system review.
  dependencies: Regional expertise, multilingual sources, affected-party participation and context-specific evidence.
  tradeoffs: The category 'Global South' can flatten major political, cultural and economic differences.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
